analysisWe need to produce an assert statement for the comment:

```
// @@@ If the collection c is not null, then every element in the priority queue is contained in the collection c.
```

Method retainAll returns boolean, but the comment states: "If the collection c is not null, then every element in the priority queue is contained in the collection c."

We need to write an assert specification that reflects that. Use \old maybe? The condition is about after operation? It says "If collection c is not null, then every element in the priority queue is contained in collection c." This is after the method execution? Usually retainAll removes elements not in c, leaving only those that are in c. So after execution, all remaining elements are in c. So assert: c != null => (\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); c.contains(this.get(i))) . Use this.get(i) to retrieve element. Or we could use iterator, but get is fine. Need to reference c (parameter) inside assert. Use c != null => ... . Use \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); c.contains(this.get(i)) . No need for old. The size after may be less or equal to old size. But condition just about containment.

Thus final code:

```java
assert c != null => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); c.contains(this.get(i));
```

Make sure syntax: parentheses around implication? Not needed but okay. Provide within <code> tags.

